    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d831">

                <pb facs="0779" n="663" sameAs="frus:frus1912/pg663"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 882.20/2.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                            American Minister</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1912-01-10">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">January 10, 1912</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>War Department thinks, on account of climate, at least four officers necessary to
                    rehabilitate border police. Has found four ex-noncommissioned officers who are
                    ready to undertake the work, provided they receive from Liberian Government
                    commissions as follows: One major, one captain, two lieutenants, with salaries
                    respectively of $2,500, $2,000, and $1,600 with housing. This must be definitely
                    settled before their departure. Cable decision Government.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Knox.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
